{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The daughter of Leah.</b> And not the daughter of Jacob? Rather, she is called the daughter of Leah on account of her going out — for she too was a woman who went out (Bereshit Rabbah), as it says ״וַתֵּצֵא לֵאָה לִקְרָאתוֹ״. And about her they coined the proverb: Like mother, like daughter."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:00.820039995Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}